## clinically-informed-support-with-you-at-the-centre | Why Clients Choose MBP | Clinically Informed Support, With You at the Centre | Why Clients Choose MBP – Clinically Informed Support, With You at the Centre
Michelle Barratt Psychology & Administration Services (MBP) provides a welcoming, neutral, and professionally managed entry point for individuals and families seeking psychological and allied health care.
- Clinically Informed Intake: Thoughtful intake processes help us understand your concerns, preferences, and accessibility needs to identify a suitable support pathway.
- Appropriate Practitioner Matching: We connect you with clinical psychologists, general psychologists, social workers, or counsellors whose experience aligns with chronic health and wellbeing support.
- Coordinated Care: Where appropriate and with your consent, practitioners can liaise with your GP, neurologist, and allied health professionals involved in your care.
- Practical Referral Support: Our team assists with GP referral requirements, Mental Health Treatment Plans, and Medicare-related paperwork where applicable.
- Flexible Access: In-person appointments are available at our Brisbane clinics in Toowong and Manly West, alongside secure Online Therapy / Telehealth Australia-wide where clinically appropriate, making sessions accessible from the comfort of home.
## you-dont-have-to-navigate-parkinsons-alone | Start with a Conversation | You Don't Have to Navigate Parkinson's Alone | Start with a Conversation – You Don't Have to Navigate Parkinson's Alone
You may not be sure whether support would be most helpful for yourself, your partner, or both of you together.
If living with Parkinson's, or supporting someone you love, has been feeling emotionally heavy and you would like a calm, non-judgmental space to talk things through, reaching out can be a helpful first step.
Tell us a little about what has been happening for you, and we will help you explore an appropriate pathway forward.
Contact Michelle Barratt Psychology on (07) 3185 0040 or reach out via our online contact form to learn more about wellbeing and psychological support.
